// `full-group.ron`'s fight, fought on a battle map instead — the same
// party, the same pack, the same seed, so the pair is the comparison.
//
// What the group model cannot see about this fight is the whole reason the
// file exists: forced focus fire disappears (only a group's front can be
// hit there; here damage spreads across whoever is in reach), and so does
// `ENGAGED_GROUPS` (a group past the second cannot act there at all unless
// it is `ranged`; here everything walks up and swings). The expectation is
// that this hits harder and swings wider than its twin.
//
// Bin only. The played arena drives rounds, so `[F]` on this file is a
// refusal naming the bin rather than a fight — see `dev-arenas/README.md`.
(
    player: Fresh(level: 20, zone: 3),
    equip: [
        (item: "plasma_router", tier: 0),
        (item: "bastion_lattice", tier: 0),
        (item: "singularity_matrix", tier: 0),
    ],
    party: [
        (species: "scrapper", level: 12, equip: [
            (item: "arc_lance"), (item: "hardened_shell"),
        ]),
        (species: "scrapper", level: 12, equip: [
            (item: "arc_lance"), (item: "hardened_shell"),
        ]),
        (species: "scrapper", level: 12, equip: [
            (item: "arc_lance"), (item: "hardened_shell"),
        ]),
    ],
    opponents: [(species: "rootkit", count: 4)],
    model: Tactical,
    // Head-on. A staged fight spawns its pack around the player, so there
    // is no tile to read a bearing off the way a real fight does; every
    // other point of the compass is the same fight from the side, which is
    // what this row is for.
    approach: Some(East),
    reps: 50,
    seed: 7,
)
